      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SOHO BELLAGIO (4) settled well back in a race that wasn't run to suit last week so did well to work home for third. Very impressive when kicking off his career with a 25m romp at Menangle prior. Has plenty of upside and this race should pan out better for him. SMACK BANG BART (7) overcame a similar barrier to this when he worked to the front and kept going to score by 3.7m in his heat. Building a handy record and won the only time he attempted this circuit and distance. LAKE COMO (10) draws on the back row but is showing some promise, placing in his two outings here to follow a debut win. FULLY RECKLESS NZ (6) draws wide than when fourth in his heat but did well to win from the back line prior. AUSTON (9) is another that may be relying on luck but he has upside and is worth including.",
